# Test Harness Pack

Use this pack when the project needs reliable test setup, fixtures, fakes, manual review checklists, playtest loops, or repeatable local verification.

## Rules

- Prefer focused tests before broad suites while iterating.
- Use fakes/mocks for platform, network, time, filesystem, and paid-service boundaries.
- Keep test data deterministic and local.
- For non-code projects, treat playtest scripts, review checklists, and component inventories as the test harness.
- Avoid arbitrary sleeps when a state-based wait or deterministic helper is available.
- Record flaky or unavailable checks instead of claiming they passed.

## Verification

- Keep `docs/ai/verification.md` current with real commands or concrete manual review/playtest checks.
- Add helper notes for common setup failures and workarounds.
